# XBD 4.3 Default Initialization
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The rules are those of the C language, which the standard requires of
# the C compiler it names. Unions are not called aggregates in the text,
# so { 0 } is tested on structures, arrays and scalars only; unions are
# tested where default initialization reaches them (as static objects and
# as members of aggregates). The padding bits are unspecified (the notes),
# so members are compared one by one.

assertion  XBD.4.3-default-initialization.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.3
class      required
says       Objects with static or thread storage duration and no initializer
           are default-initialized: pointers are null, integers, booleans,
           enumerations and complex numbers zero, floating members positive
           zero, every member of a structure or array likewise (nested
           ones too), a union by its first named member; this holds for
           file-scope, external and function-scope static objects.
test       t/001-static-default.c

assertion  XBD.4.3-default-initialization.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.3
class      required
says       An initializer of { 0 } default-initializes a structure or array
           (nested aggregates, floating members, pointers, a union member,
           character arrays) of automatic, static or thread storage
           duration, and the compound literal { 0 } assigned over dirty
           memory; an automatic one is fresh on every pass of a loop.
test       t/002-braces-zero.c

assertion  XBD.4.3-default-initialization.003
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.3
class      required
says       Initializers apply in list order and a later one for the same
           subobject replaces an earlier one: repeated member designators,
           array designators that re-aim the position, nested designators
           and array-of-structure designators leave the last value, and
           the elements and members never named are zero.
test       t/003-list-order.c

assertion  XBD.4.3-default-initialization.004
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.3
class      required
says       Members of a structure that its initializer (by designator or by
           position) does not name are default-initialized: null pointers,
           positive zero for floating members, the first named member of a
           union member, the remaining characters of a string-initialized
           array and the unnamed elements of nested arrays of structures.
test       t/004-implicit-rest.c

assertion  XBD.4.3-default-initialization.005
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.3
class      required
says       An initializer of { 0 } on a scalar of automatic or static
           storage (integer, boolean, enumeration, floating types, object
           and function pointers) gives it zero, positive zero or a null
           pointer.
test       t/005-braces-scalar.c

assertion  XBD.4.3-default-initialization.006
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.3
class      required
says       Where the all-zero bit pattern of float, double and long double is
           positive zero (it must be wherever __STDC_IEC_559__ is defined,
           the only case in which the test can fail on that point), a
           structure zeroed by memset() or allocated by calloc() has the same
           member values as one default-initialized. NOTINUSE where the
           macro is not defined and the pattern is not positive zero.
test       t/006-zero-bits.c
